{"source":"I walked past the old skating rink this morning on my way to the bakery. The sign is gone, but the blue doors are still there, with the same dent near the handle. I hadn't thought about that place in years. Then I remembered waiting outside in wet socks after Saturday lessons because my brother and I were sure our parents would be late. They never were. We just had no patience for standing still once the music stopped.

I nearly took a photo, but there was a delivery van parked in front and I was carrying a bag that had started to split. Maybe I'll go back with a camera next weekend, if the weather holds. I don't know what they use the building for now. It might be nothing interesting to anyone else, but I would like one picture of those doors before somebody paints them.","candidate":"I walked past the old skating rink this morning on my way to the bakery. The sign is gone, but the blue doors are still there, with the same dent near the handle. I hadn't thought about that place in years. Then I remembered waiting outside in wet socks after Saturday lessons, because my brother and I were sure our parents would be late. They never were. We just had no patience for standing still once the music stopped.

