{"source":"Saturday's repair café had a good turnout. The bike table stayed busy until the last half hour, and the sewing corner had a steady line after lunch. A few people came just to watch, then ended up helping someone else figure out a loose hinge or a stuck zipper. That part felt nice: nobody seemed in a hurry to leave once their own thing was fixed.

Thanks to the volunteers who brought tools and to the folks who waited patiently. We had a couple of small bottlenecks, especially at the sewing machine, but people made room for one another. Next month we may add a second sewing station if we can find another machine. If you have one we could borrow for the afternoon, let us know; we haven't settled the setup yet, so for now that's just an idea.","candidate":"Saturday's repair café had a good turnout. The bike table stayed busy until the last half hour, and the sewing corner had a steady line after lunch. A few people came just to watch, then ended up helping someone else figure out a loose hinge or a stuck zipper. That part felt nice: nobody seemed in a hurry to leave once their own thing was fixed.

